# Resolve open questions → specs

When Product (or the user) **answers** an open question — HQ ledger or [OPEN_QUESTIONS.md](docs/context/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md) — do **not** leave it as **Resolved** on an open list.

## Same-turn checklist

1. **Write the decision into the owning specs** as product truth (e.g. INTERACTIONS, UX_SPEC, FEATURE_MATRIX, COMPONENTS, VIEW_DATA_REQUIREMENTS, co-located `*.spec.md`, format docs). Prefer normative wording (“does / does not”), not “until Q*”.
2. **Update the open list(s)** in the **same change**:
   - [OPEN_QUESTIONS.md](docs/context/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md) — **delete** the P0/P1/P2 table row; optional one-line **resolution log** entry pointing at the specs (not at HQ).
   - [HQ_OPEN_QUESTIONS.md](docs/context/HQ_OPEN_QUESTIONS.md) — **keep** the Q block; tag **ANSWERED** (and **Implemented** when shipped). Do not leave a bare Open/Interim answer only in chat.
3. **Clear dependents** in the same change: strike matching [INTERIM_DECISIONS.md](docs/context/INTERIM_DECISIONS.md) rows; drop “until Q*” / “blocked on Q*” wording in docs, specs, and code comments.
4. **Tests** — if behavior is already implemented, assert the decided rule; if not, leave the spec as the requirement for the next slice.

## Obsolete (sketch / product retired the ask)

When UI chrome is removed or renamed (e.g. v930 refresh):

1. Tag the retired ask **OBSOLETE** on the HQ ledger (one-line note; keep crop).
2. Sync OPEN_QUESTIONS / INTERIM so they do not still treat the old chrome as an open Product ask.
3. Do not invent formulas for replacement labels until Product answers the new question.

## Do not

- Leave a **Resolved** row sitting in an OPEN_QUESTIONS table
- Answer only in chat without specs + list sync
- Keep interim “guess until Product answers” text after Product answered
- Re-open **OBSOLETE** layout questions (ask the new labels instead)

Canonical process: [DEVELOPMENT.md](docs/process/DEVELOPMENT.md) § Resolving open questions.
